import json,sys
s=json.loads(Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text());out=Path(sys.argv[2]);p=s['primary'];before=p['medians']['before'];after=p['medians']['after'];comparison=p['comparisons']['after_over_before'];families=s['allocation_comparison']
lines=['# R65: inline the maintained checked-debit helper','',f"Candidate build: `{s['static']['after']['source']}`. Baseline R64 build: `{s['static']['before']['source']}`. Accepted baseline checkpoint: `{s['baseline_provenance']['accepted_checkpoint']}`.",'',f"The complete eight-byte level-12 call measured **{after['multiple_of_reference']:.6f}× the reference**, from **{before['multiple_of_reference']:.6f}×** in this matched baseline cohort. Candidate/baseline elapsed: **{comparison['pooled_ratio']:.8f}×** ({s['changes_percent']['primary_seconds']:+.4f}%). The freshly measured reference median was {p['reference_seconds']*1000:.6f} ms.",'','The sole production change replaces `#[inline]` with `#[inline(always)]` on `NativeLibraryWorkBudget::charge_in_context`. It exposes the existing maintained checked-debit body to its callers, including a constant zero comparison delta in the compute-only path. Accounting arithmetic, current account/TLS access, finite limits, error precedence and debit order remain source-identical. Existing parent and candidate tests cover finite ceiling/overflow before foreign-account rejection, tighter library caps, unchanged work on denial and successful retry. No new semantic implementation or source test is introduced.','', 'Engine, Compute, Stdlib, Runtime and GPU were rebuilt coherently with their retained flags/features and warnings-as-errors. Core, math, syntax and external artifacts remain frozen. The candidate emits its Object, descriptor and metadata afresh; all three must match the R64 baseline byte-for-byte. No compressor source, algorithm, source allocation site or timing boundary changes.','', '| Metric | Reference | R64 baseline | R65 candidate | Change |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|',f"| Primary elapsed (ms) | {p['reference_seconds']*1000:.6f} | {before['seconds']*1000:.6f} | {after['seconds']*1000:.6f} | {s['changes_percent']['primary_seconds']:+.4f}% |"]
for section,key,label in [('cpu','instructions','Retired instructions'),('cpu','cycles','CPU cycles'),('allocation','allocation_requests','Allocation requests'),('allocation','requested_bytes','Requested bytes'),('allocation','reallocations','Reallocations'),('allocation','peak_live_usable','Peak allocator live usable bytes'),('allocation','incremental_peak_live_usable','Incremental allocator peak'),('cpu','rss_after','RSS after call'),('cpu','physical_after','Physical footprint after call')]:
 values=[s[section][variant][key]['median'] for variant in ['reference','before','after']];change=s['changes_percent'][key]
 lines.append('| '+label+' | '+' | '.join(f'{v:,.1f}' if int(v)!=v else f'{v:,.0f}' for v in values)+' | '+('—' if change is None else f'{change:+.4f}%')+' |')
lines+=['','Primary elapsed, CPU counters, heap counters and CPU-time samples are separate serial cohorts. Their percentages are not multiplied or combined. Requested bytes represent allocation requests, not initialized bytes copied. Allocator peak and post-call OS footprint are different measures; the latter is not peak RSS and includes retained compiler/catalog/image storage.','', '## Allocation and instruction mechanism','', 'This attribute-only change predicts zero successful-call allocation savings. It targets checked-debit call/return, constant-argument and result transport costs. The actual emitted host code determines what disappears; the directive itself is not evidence. Hardware instruction changes are measured independently of allocator counts and CPU-time samples.','', '| Complete census | R64 baseline | R65 candidate | Delta |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for key,label in [('requests','Allocation requests'),('requested_bytes','Requested bytes'),('reallocations','Reallocations')]:
 lines.append(f"| {label} | {families['before'][key]:,} | {families['after'][key]:,} | {families['whole_call_delta'][key]:+,} |")
lines+=['',f"Size/kind request histogram unchanged: **{families['size_kind_histogram_unchanged']}**. Both full censuses are fresh R65 measurements, individually reconciled to their separate eight-observation heap cohorts. The archived trace pins and per-size counts are in `allocation-comparison.json`. Equal totals do not establish identical work or execution counts.",'', 'Earlier sample and host-code evidence identified the checked-debit caller/callee boundary. R64 already addressed the separate full-policy-evaluator query. No R64 gain is reproposed or included here. TLS source is unchanged; earlier TLS sample weights are not treated as removable by this attribute.','', '## Matched pairs and adverse observations','', '| Pair | Baseline ms | Candidate ms | Candidate/baseline |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
